<article class="env-lemma" id="0DZL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DZL">Lemma <span data-tag="0DZL">93.8.4</span>.</a> In Example <a href="/tag/0DY1" data-tag="0DY1">93.8.1</a> let $P$ be a smooth $k$-algebra. Then $T\mathcal{D}\! \mathit{ef}_ P = (0)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0DY3" data-tag="0DY3">93.8.3</a> we have to show $\text{Ext}^1_ P(\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{P/k}, P) = (0)$. Since $k \to P$ is smooth $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{P/k}$ is quasi-isomorphic to the complex consisting of a finite projective $P$-module placed in degree $0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>